= Kolchak's Coup

On 18 November, officers loyal to Admiral Alexander Kolchak arrested the SR members of the Directory in Omsk, the anti-Bolshevik government that had been formed in Ufa in September from the SR and Kadet delegates. Kolchak proclaimed himself Supreme Ruler. The SRs who had joined the anti-Bolshevik cause, among them Avksentiev and Zenzinov, were deported to the West.

The other side of the civil war has now shown its hand. A White Russia would be a dictatorship of the officers, and the socialists, of every party, would be in prison.

For the Mensheviks it is a sign that the policy of "neither side" is not so foolish after all, and that armed struggle against the Bolsheviks can only help the Whites.
